Session 5 summary — criteria NOT met (no marker written); major root-cause progress with two failure families fully solved and the third cornered to its manufacture site:

**Solved this session (all RULE-4 proven, fixes landed v0.10.17→0.10.23, build 345C285B deployed):**
1. **The uv "16 ghost files" failure** — platter decode proved the ghosts are leafless dirents: create-wave leaf wars drop leaf-hash entries; `rm` of a hole-name ENOENTs at the leaf, the unlink txn aborts, `rm -f` swallows it, and the dirent bytes + live inode survive. Fixed with `mxfs_dir2_leafless_removename` (P73): on leaf-ENOENT, scan data blocks and expunge the dirent data-side so the unlink completes. Verified firing (3×/run) and the got=16 face is gone.
2. **Datascan corruption storms** — the datascan (and my new remover) read legally-sparse dirs without `XFS_DABUF_MAP_HOLE_OK`, so every hole raised `xfs_corruption_error` + marked the dir sick, killing whole mv waves (proven test4). Fixed by passing HOLE_OK in both + gating the P14 probe to non-HOLE_OK callers (most "P14 storms" were benign readdir holes).
3. **The remaining blocker cornered in the act**: the `i != 1` shutdown in `xfs_bmap_del_extent_real` during renames. New P75/P75b probes at the crash site proved the in-core iext holds a committed mapping (e.g. `[10,4]`) while the bmbt leaf == LUN holds the pre-commit shape (`[11,3]`) — and the new P76 probe caught `P61-CHOKEPOINT-SKIP-BMBT` fake-completing writes **whose content differs from the LUN** on the same owner/daddr seconds before the crash: the skip retires the BLI and stamps written_seq, so the committed bmbt update silently never lands; a later evict re-reads the stale LUN and the node's bmbt time-travels behind its own iext.

**Next session's queued fix (design in memory `AAA-ccloop46ef-sess5-END-P61-skip-eats-bmbt-commits-fix-design`):** at the P61 skip, when content differs from the LUN, bump `b_mxfs_logged_seq` (mark undestaged) instead of lying — existing guards then protect the in-core truth and the next EX tenure's fence lands it; plus verify the bast_process drain path consults the bmbt scan before unlock. Then cache_coherency@32 ×2 green → trio → dir_reuse → the full 1/2/4/8/16/32 ladder.

